<!--
    loweredswitch: the re-rolled switch must dispatch on the value the cascade
    compared, and the function must keep the parameter that value came from.

    `loweredswitch` (DIV-4, default on) detects a compiler-lowered comparison
    cascade on the simplified CFG and then installs a synthesized BRANCHIND plus
    JumpTable pre-SSA, on the re-lifted p-code of a restart.  The synthesized
    BRANCHIND has to reach the rest of the pipeline as a live op: an op that is
    not on the alive list is skipped by the dead-code consume propagation, so
    nothing records that the BRANCHIND reads its selector, and the selector is
    then folded to the constant 0 (or swept outright, leaving the un-compilable
    `switch()`).  The cases and the binary-search tree shape survive either way,
    so a corpus that asserts only case labels cannot see the difference - which
    is why the assertions here are about the scrutinee.

    Stage model: S2 "switch-model" sub-stage.  P0 assertion: `option
    loweredswitch on|off`.

    Layout (x86:LE:64, flat at 0x100000) - the /Od shape the compiler emits for
    a four-way sparse switch: the parameter is spilled to its home slot and every
    comparison reads the slot back.

      swfn @ 0x100000 :  sub  rsp,0x28
                         mov  [rsp+8],edi        ; spill the parameter
                         cmp  [rsp+8],0x2003 / je / jl
                         cmp  [rsp+8],0x3007 / je / jl
                         cmp  [rsp+8],0x400b / je / jl
                         cmp  [rsp+8],0x1000 / je / jl
                         (four one-line case bodies and a default)

    Pass 1 (option loweredswitch off): the compiler's own if/else-if chain over
    the parameter, which is what the re-roll has to agree with.
    Pass 2 (option loweredswitch on - the shipped default): one switch over that
    same parameter.

    Asserts #1/#2 are the regression pins: the scrutinee is the parameter, and it
    is never the constant 0 nor missing.  #3 pins the parameter into both
    prototypes - before the fix the re-rolled pass rendered `swfn(void)` because
    the folded selector left nothing reading it.  #4/#5 pin the recovered case
    labels, #6 the chain that pass 1 keeps, and #7 a case body shared by both.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
